---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import catalog from '../data/catalog.json';
import { CATEGORIES } from '../lib/catalog.ts';
import tools from '../data/ai-tools.json';
const featured = catalog.slice(0, 8);
const cats = CATEGORIES.filter((c) => catalog.some((e) => e.category === c.slug));
const featuredTools = tools.slice(0, 6);
---
<BaseLayout title="PARADOX — AI agent intelligence and trust signals" description="Discover, inspect, compare and evaluate public AI agents and GitHub projects using observable repository evidence before you depend on them.">
  <main class="paradox-home">
    <section class="hero-home">
      <div class="hero-home-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">AI AGENT INTELLIGENCE / TRUST SIGNALS / 01</p>
        <h1>Understand the agents you are about to <em>trust.</em></h1>
        <p class="lead">Discover public AI agents and GitHub projects, then inspect observable evidence for activity, health, documentation, stack and static risk signals before you depend on them.</p>
        <form class="search-row" method="get" action="/agents/">
          <label class="visually-hidden" for="homeQuery">Search AI agents</label>
          <input id="homeQuery" name="q" type="search" placeholder="Search agents, skills, repositories, MCP…" />
          <button type="submit"><span>Explore</span></button>
        </form>
        <div class="sub-actions"><a href="/verify/">Inspect a GitHub repository →</a><a href="/compare/">Compare two agents →</a></div>
        <div class="cats" aria-label="Agent categories">{cats.map((c) => <a href={`/categories/${c.slug}/`}>{c.label}</a>)}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="pv-hero-visual" aria-label="PARADOX agent intelligence network visualization">
        <div class="pv-orbit"></div><div class="pv-core"><strong>PX</strong></div>
        <div class="pv-node n1"><b>REPOSITORY</b><span>evidence indexed</span></div>
        <div class="pv-node n2"><b>RISK SIGNAL</b><span>static scan</span></div>
        <div class="pv-node n3"><b>FRESHNESS</b><span>activity signal</span></div>
        <div class="pv-node n4"><b>STACK</b><span>dependencies</span></div>
        <div class="pv-wave"></div><div class="pv-scan"><span>INTELLIGENCE STATUS <strong>ONLINE</strong></span><span>OBSERVABLE EVIDENCE</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pv-stats" aria-label="Platform principles">
      <div class="pv-stat"><span>Decision model</span><strong>EVIDENCE FIRST</strong><em>NO GUESSING</em></div>
      <div class="pv-stat"><span>Inspection mode</span><strong>NO EXECUTION</strong><em>DATA ONLY</em></div>
      <div class="pv-stat"><span>Core signals</span><strong>HEALTH / ACTIVITY</strong><em>LIVE CHECK</em></div>
      <div class="pv-stat"><span>Decision layer</span><strong>VERIFY / COMPARE</strong><em>READY</em></div>
    </section>

    <section class="ai-product-section" id="ai-tools">
      <div class="ai-product-copy">
        <span class="pv-section-label">02 / AI WORKBENCH</span>
        <h2>Actual AI tools.<br /><em>Not another AI landing page.</em></h2>
        <p>Use PARADOX to do real work: tailor a resume, prepare for an interview, turn notes into a study pack, generate content, fix code and use focused AI developer utilities.</p>
        <div class="ai-product-actions"><a href="/ai/" class="ai-product-primary">OPEN AI TOOLS ↗</a><a href="/ai-studio/">Launch AI Studio</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ai-tool-grid-home">
        {featuredTools.map((tool, i) => (
          <a class="ai-tool-card-home" href={`/ai/${tool.slug}/`}>
            <span>{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <strong>{tool.label}</strong>
            <p>{tool.description}</p>
            <b>USE TOOL ↗</b>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="si-trust-grid" aria-label="What PARADOX evaluates">
        <article class="si-trust-card"><span>01 / MAINTENANCE</span><strong>Is it alive?</strong><p>Freshness, commits, releases and contributor activity help reveal whether a project is still maintained.</p></article>
        <article class="si-trust-card"><span>02 / ENGINEERING</span><strong>What is inside?</strong><p>Stack files, languages, models and tools are surfaced from observable repository evidence.</p></article>
        <article class="si-trust-card"><span>03 / RISK</span><strong>What stands out?</strong><p>Static risk indicators expose patterns worth investigating without executing the repository.</p></article>
        <article class="si-trust-card"><span>04 / DECISION</span><strong>Which should I choose?</strong><p>Compare repositories using the same evidence model instead of relying on popularity alone.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" style="padding-top:20px">
      <div class="si-decision">
        <div><span class="pv-section-label">03 / THE WORKFLOW</span><h2>From discovery to a defensible decision.</h2><p class="si-lead">PARADOX is designed to make an agent understandable before it becomes a dependency. Every step leads back to observable repository evidence.</p></div>
        <div class="si-steps" aria-label="PARADOX workflow">
          <div class="si-step"><b>01</b><strong>Discover</strong><span>find candidates</span><em>CATALOG + SEARCH</em></div>
          <div class="si-step"><b>02</b><strong>Inspect</strong><span>read the evidence</span><em>HEALTH + STACK</em></div>
          <div class="si-step"><b>03</b><strong>Compare</strong><span>normalize signals</span><em>SIDE BY SIDE</em></div>
          <div class="si-step"><b>04</b><strong>Decide</strong><span>keep uncertainty visible</span><em>UNKNOWN ≠ SAFE</em></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="si-profile-band"><div><h3>Built for the agent ecosystem, not just one scanner.</h3><p>Security is one signal. PARADOX combines trust, maintenance, engineering and activity signals into one intelligence profile so builders can evaluate an agent before depending on it.</p></div><div class="si-pills"><span class="si-pill">Agent registry</span><span class="si-pill">Repository intelligence</span><span class="si-pill">Trust signals</span><span class="si-pill">Evidence graph</span></div></div>
    </section>

    <section class="section"><div class="pv-section-head"><div><span class="pv-section-label">04 / CURATED SIGNALS</span><h2>Featured agents.</h2></div><p>Start with public systems already catalogued by PARADOX, then inspect the evidence behind each profile.</p></div><div class="grid-2">{featured.map((e) => (<article class="agent-card"><div class="meta"><span>{e.owner}</span><span>{e.category}</span></div><h3>{e.repo}</h3><p>{e.summary}</p><div class="links"><a href={`/agents/${e.owner}/${e.repo}/`}>Open profile</a><a href={`/verify/?url=${encodeURIComponent(`https://github.com/${e.owner}/${e.repo}`)}`}>Verify</a></div></article>))}</div></section>
    <section class="section" style="padding-top:0"><div class="pv-section-head"><div><span class="pv-section-label">05 / RECENT ACTIVITY</span><h2>Recently catalogued.</h2></div><p>New repositories enter the catalog as discoverable starting points. Live health signals are checked when you inspect them.</p></div><div class="grid-2">{catalog.slice(8).map((e) => (<article class="agent-card"><div class="meta"><span>{e.owner}/{e.repo}</span></div><h3>{e.repo}</h3><p>{e.summary}</p><div class="links"><a href={`/agents/${e.owner}/${e.repo}/`}>Open profile</a></div></article>))}</div></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
<style>.visually-hidden{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;padding:0;margin:-1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0,0,0,0);border:0}</style>
